## Why

Real tender lines often combine a procurement action with an otherwise useful product description. The current canonical alternate can retain the work wording, while previous attempts to infer missing product facts, suppress vendor text, or route action-bearing lines to `NOT_FOUND` were unsafe. A narrowly extracted product span can test whether the product evidence is recoverable without treating service language as evidence of catalog absence.

## What Changes

- Add a deterministic product-span retrieval alternate for a narrowly recognized mixed work-and-product tender clause.
- Use the alternate only in addition to the unchanged raw tender line; retain existing hybrid limits, RRF merging, reranker input, result query, and final selection behavior.
- Require an explicit work cue and an explicit supported purchasable-product anchor in the same clause; retain adjacent technical text and decline to create a span when boundaries or product evidence are ambiguous.
- Keep service-only, unsupported, and non-action product lines on their current retrieval path.
- Add focused tests for valid mixed clauses, preservation of product constraints, no-op conditions, retrieval call behavior, and fail-open operation.

## Capabilities

### New Capabilities

- `mixed-line-product-retrieval`: Produces a bounded additive retrieval representation for explicit purchasable products embedded in tender work descriptions.

### Modified Capabilities

- None.

## Impact

- Affected package code: `query_canonicalization.py`, `matcher.py`, and, only if needed to carry the alternate, `hybrid_retriever.py`.
- Affected tests: canonicalization, matcher query preservation, and mocked hybrid retrieval tests.
- No new providers, catalog/index schema, embeddings, Qdrant collection, or index rebuild. The outer harness owns regression evaluation and promotion.

